From k10-k12 (skill-author). A section named like a Windows device (aux.md, con.md, nul.md) makes filepath.IsLocal fail on Windows 10 (RtlIsDosDeviceName_U), so isPlainName rejects it and the whole skill set is skipped with only a WARN, leaving the previous start's files on disk. Linux tests cannot see it and Windows 11 accepts the name. Fix: reject such section names in checkSkillDirs (cmd/launcher/skills.go) on every platform, reusing reservedDeviceName from k76 (filetools.go), with a test over a fake set; the unreagent-skill-authoring skill already tells authors not to use them. Lane: unreagent-worker. No shipped skill has such a section today.

